#. +> trunk5
#: ../../effects_and_compositions/video_effects/on_master/audio_spectrum_filter.rst:36
msgid "**Graph type** - Select the type of graph to display the levels. Option are **Line** (default) and **Bar**."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: ../../effects_and_compositions/video_effects/on_master/audio_spectrum_filter.rst:38
msgid "**Fill** - If checked, fills the area under the graph. Only applies to :guilabel:`Graph type` **Line**."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: ../../effects_and_compositions/video_effects/on_master/audio_spectrum_filter.rst:40
msgid "**Mirror** - If checked, mirrors the spectrum on the center line of the rectangle"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: ../../effects_and_compositions/video_effects/on_master/audio_spectrum_filter.rst:42
msgid "**Reverse** - If checked, draws the points starting with the highest frequency"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: ../../effects_and_compositions/video_effects/on_master/audio_spectrum_filter.rst:44
msgid "**Window size** - The number of samples that the FFT\\ [1]_ will be performed on. If :guilabel:`Window size` is less than the number of samples in a frame, extra samples will be ignored. If :guilabel:`Window size` is more than the number of samples in a frame, samples will be buffered from previous frames to fill the window. The buffering is performed as a sliding window so that the most recent samples are always transformed."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: ../../effects_and_compositions/video_effects/on_master/audio_spectrum_filter.rst:46
msgid "**Background Color** - Defines the background color to be applied to the entire frame"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: ../../effects_and_compositions/video_effects/on_master/audio_spectrum_filter.rst:48
msgid "**Foreground color** - Defines the color of the waveform"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: ../../effects_and_compositions/video_effects/on_master/audio_spectrum_filter.rst:50
msgid "**Line Thickness** - Defines the thickness of the bar or line in number of pixels"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: ../../effects_and_compositions/video_effects/on_master/audio_spectrum_filter.rst:52
msgid "**Angle** - Defines the rotation angle to be applied to the waveform"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: ../../effects_and_compositions/video_effects/on_master/audio_spectrum_filter.rst:54
msgid "**X / Y / W / H / Size / Opacity** - Defines the X and Y coordinates, Width and Height, Size and Opacity of the rectangle in which the waveform is drawn. The icons help in lining up the rectangle."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: ../../effects_and_compositions/video_effects/on_master/audio_spectrum_filter.rst:56
msgid "**Line Tension** - Affects the amount of curve in the line interpolating between points. **0** draws a straight line between points; **100** draws very curved lines between points. Values below **0** and above **100** will cause loops in the lines. Only applies to :guilabel:`Graph type` **Line**."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: ../../effects_and_compositions/video_effects/on_master/audio_spectrum_filter.rst:58
msgid "**Points** - Defines the number of bands to draw in the spectrum. Each band shows up as a data point in the graph."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: ../../effects_and_compositions/video_effects/on_master/audio_spectrum_filter.rst:63
msgid "The effect is not updated in the Project Monitor during scrubbing. You need to play back the project to see this effect."
msgstr ""

